  "description": "Draws CodeBrix.VideoPlayback frames through SkiaSharp. SkiaVideoPresenter takes the newest decoded frame and composes it on an off-screen surface - on the GPU through one SkSL shader that does YUV-to-RGB and a resultant colour LUT in a single pass, or on the CPU through the core's SIMD converter - then blits the result into whatever canvas the application owns, with letterboxing, drawable overlay layers and a composed-frame capture. Plain SkiaSharp only: no view package, no native asset, no windowing dependency.",
